      options: ["Assume no transport changes are needed since stdio should work exactly the same once it is exposed over a public network", "Move to Streamable HTTP with OAuth 2.1 authorization, since stdio only suits a local single-client subprocess", "Keep writing debug logs to stdout for both versions, assuming stdio always logs there safely", "Assume remote MCP servers are simply unable to support any form of authentication"],
